{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And this for Judah.</b> And this blessing itself shall take effect upon Judah. Here Rashi explained: Moses said — what caused Reuben to confess? Judah. And if you ask: is not Reuben's confession prior to Judah's, for in the portion of וישב, concerning ״וישב ראובן אל הבור״, Rashi explained that he was not present at the sale, for he was occupied with his sackcloth and his fasting, and Judah did not confess until Tamar conceived? One may answer: indeed Reuben confessed first, but he confessed privately — in his sackcloth and in his fasting; but publicly he did not confess. And when Judah confessed and said ״צדקה ממני,״ Reuben arose and publicized his confession and said, ״אף אני בלבלתי יצועי אבי.״ And a proof for this: that Moses our Teacher juxtaposed the blessing of Judah to the blessing of Reuben, because through Judah, Reuben confessed an important and publicized confession. This is what it says: what caused Reuben to confess publicly — Judah." "<b>Hear, O YHWH, the voice of Judah.</b> When he cries out in war and needs aid. And since Judah goes up first to war, it was necessary to pray for him regarding the needs of war, and for Reuben as well, because Reuben crossed first, as it is written, ״והחלוץ עבר לפניהם.״ But Simeon there was no need to mention here, because he was accustomed to go with Judah, as it is written in the book of Judges, ״עלה אתי בגורלי.״ Another interpretation, ״יחי ראובן״: because he sinned against his father's honor, and he deserved to die, as it is written, ״כבד את אביך למען יאריכון ימיך״ — hence, if you do not honor him, your days will be shortened; therefore he said, ״ואל ימות.״" "<b>And this for Judah.</b> This blessing itself shall be thus for Judah — for in this matter he sinned, that he distressed his father with the tunic of Joseph. And Simeon he did not wish to mention in a blessing, because it was in Moses' heart on account of his having been first in the selling of Joseph, as Rashi explained in the portion of מקץ."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {0 "The abbreviation פירש״י is resolved as 'Rashi explained,' following the compiler's convention of citing Rashi without naming him; the text as given here explicitly writes the name.", 2 "The abbreviation פירש״י is resolved as 'Rashi explained,' consistent with comment [0]; the text here also explicitly writes the name."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:55:27.916105652Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}